IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nmw-types`

-- National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK) — GOAL 1: WHO QUALIFIES.
--
--   "Does this individual qualify for the national minimum wage for this
--    work?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1998-39.txt — ss 1, 3, 28, 34,
-- 35, 37, 37A, 40, 43-45B, 54.

§ `Goal 1 — who qualifies`

§§ `The presumption (s 28(1))`

-- s 28(1) "Where in any civil proceedings any question arises as to whether
-- an individual qualifies or qualified at any time for the national minimum
-- wage, it shall be presumed that the individual qualifies or, as the case
-- may be, qualified at that time for the national minimum wage unless the
-- contrary is established." Outside civil proceedings there is no
-- presumption, and a condition not established either way is refused.
@ref s 28(1)
GIVEN fact IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, civil IS A BOOLEAN, what IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`established, or presumed under s 28(1)` fact `in civil proceedings` civil `as to` what MEANS
    CONSIDER fact
    WHEN JUST b  THEN b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF civil THEN TRUE
        ELSE `not established, and outside civil proceedings` what

GIVEN what IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`not established, and outside civil proceedings` what MEANS
    REFUSE "s 28(1) presumes qualification only in civil proceedings; this condition is not established"

§§ `The three conditions (s 1(2))`

-- s 54(3) "worker" ... "means an individual who has entered into or works
-- under (or, where the employment has ceased, worked under)— (a) a contract
-- of employment; or (b) any other contract ... whereby the individual
-- undertakes to do or perform personally any work or services for another
-- party to the contract whose status is not by virtue of the contract that
-- of a client or customer". s 34(2): "the other provisions of this Act shall
-- have effect as if there were a worker's contract" for an agency worker.
-- s 35(1): for a home worker, "personally" reads "(whether personally or
-- otherwise)".
@ref ss 1(2)(a), 34, 35, 54(3)
GIVEN q IS A `Qualification facts`, civil IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a worker` q `in civil proceedings` civil IF
        q's `an agency worker within s 34`
    OR  q's `a home worker within s 35`
    OR  `established, or presumed under s 28(1)` (q's `has a worker's contract`) `in civil proceedings` civil `as to` "worker"

-- s 40 "an individual employed to work on board a ship registered in the
-- United Kingdom under Part II of the Merchant Shipping Act 1995 shall be
-- treated as an individual who under his contract ordinarily works in the
-- United Kingdom unless— (a) the employment is wholly outside the United
-- Kingdom; or (b) the person is not ordinarily resident in the United
-- Kingdom".
@ref ss 1(2)(b), 40
GIVEN q IS A `Qualification facts`, civil IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `works in the United Kingdom` q `in civil proceedings` civil IF
        (    q's `employed on a ship registered in the United Kingdom`
         AND NOT q's `the employment is wholly outside the United Kingdom`
         AND q's `ordinarily resident in the United Kingdom`)
    OR  `established, or presumed under s 28(1)` (q's `working or ordinarily working in the United Kingdom`) `in civil proceedings` civil `as to` "UK"

§§ `The exclusions (ss 3, 37, 37A, 43, 44, 44A, 45, 45A, 45B)`

-- s 44(1) "A worker employed by a charity, a voluntary organisation, an
-- associated fund-raising body or a statutory body does not qualify ... if he
-- receives, and under the terms of his employment (apart from this Act) is
-- entitled to,— (a) no monetary payments of any description, or no monetary
-- payments except in respect of expenses ...; and (b) no benefits in kind of
-- any description, or no benefits in kind other than the provision of some
-- or all of his subsistence or of such accommodation as is reasonable". (2)
-- money "made solely for the purpose of providing him with means of
-- subsistence" does not stop it, where "(a) he is employed ... as a result of
-- arrangements made between a charity acting in pursuance of its charitable
-- purposes and the body for which the work is done; and (b) the work is done
-- for a charity, a voluntary organisation, an associated fund-raising body or
-- a statutory body".
@ref s 44
GIVEN v IS A `Voluntary work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a voluntary worker under s 44` v IF
        v's `employed by a charity, voluntary organisation, associated fund-raising body or statutory body`
    AND v's `receives and is entitled to no money except expenses, apart from any money solely for subsistence`
    AND (   (NOT v's `also receives money solely for subsistence`)
         OR v's `placed by a charity with such a body`)
    AND v's `receives and is entitled to no benefits in kind except subsistence or reasonable accommodation`

-- s 44A "(1) A residential member of a community to which this section
-- applies does not qualify ... in respect of employment by the community.
-- (2) ... this section applies to a community if— (a) it is a charity or is
-- established by a charity, (b) a purpose of the community is to practise or
-- advance a belief of a religious or similar nature, and (c) all or some of
-- its members live together for that purpose. (3) This section does not
-- apply to a community which— (a) is an independent school or an
-- alternative provision Academy ..., or (b) provides a course of further or
-- higher education."
@ref s 44A
GIVEN c IS A `Community facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a resident member of a religious community under s 44A` c IF
        c's `a residential member of a community employing them`
    AND c's `the community is or was established by a charity`
    AND c's `a purpose is to practise or advance a religious or similar belief`
    AND c's `members live together for that purpose`
    AND NOT c's `a school or a provider of further or higher education`

-- s 37(1) "does not qualify ... in respect of that service"; s 37A "does
-- not qualify ... in respect of anything done by him in so assisting"; s 43
-- "remunerated, in respect of that employment, only by a share in the
-- profits or gross earnings of the vessel, does not qualify"; s 45(1) "in
-- respect of any work which he does in pursuance of prison rules"; s 45A "in
-- respect of any work that he does in pursuance of a work order"; s 45B
-- (Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 s 153A).
@ref ss 37, 37A, 43, 45, 45A, 45B
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is excluded` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `ordinary work` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `on a fishing vessel` shareOnly THEN shareOnly
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@ref ss 3(2)(a), 37, 37A, 43, 44, 44A, 45, 45A, 45B
GIVEN q IS A `Qualification facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is excluded from the national minimum wage` q IF
        `the work is excluded` (q's `the kind of work`)
    OR  `is a voluntary worker under s 44` (q's `voluntary work`)
    OR  `is a resident member of a religious community under s 44A` (q's `community`)
    OR  q's `prevented from qualifying by regulations under s 3`

§§ `Qualification (s 1(2))`

-- s 1 "(2) A person qualifies for the national minimum wage if he is an
-- individual who— (a) is a worker; (b) is working, or ordinarily works, in
-- the United Kingdom under his contract; and (c) has ceased to be of
-- compulsory school age." (5) "Subsections (1) to (4) above are subject to
-- the following provisions of this Act."
@ref ss 1(2), 1(5), 28(1)
@export Whether an individual qualifies for the national minimum wage under s 1(2) of the National Minimum Wage Act 1998 (UK): a worker (including an agency worker under s 34 and a home worker under s 35), working or ordinarily working in the UK (a mariner on a UK-registered ship under s 40), past compulsory school age, and not excluded (armed forces s 37, cadet volunteers s 37A, share fishermen s 43, voluntary workers s 44, residential religious communities s 44A, prisoners s 45, fine work orders s 45A, immigration detainees s 45B, or s 3 regulations). In civil proceedings a condition not established either way is presumed met (s 28(1)); outside them it is refused. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN q IS A `Qualification facts`  @desc The worker's contract (NOTHING if not established), agency or home worker status, work in the UK and the mariner facts, school age, s 3 regulations, the kind of work, and the voluntary-work and community facts
      civil IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the question arises in civil proceedings (an employment tribunal or another civil court), where s 28(1) presumes qualification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies for the national minimum wage` q `in civil proceedings` civil IF
        `is a worker` q `in civil proceedings` civil
    AND `works in the United Kingdom` q `in civil proceedings` civil
    AND `established, or presumed under s 28(1)` (q's `has ceased to be of compulsory school age`) `in civil proceedings` civil `as to` "school age"
    AND NOT (`is excluded from the national minimum wage` q)

-- Whether the question can be answered without refusing: in civil
-- proceedings always (s 28(1)); outside them, when an exclusion is
-- established or each condition of s 1(2) is established either way (a
-- worker by s 34 or s 35, the United Kingdom by s 40). Added after the
-- independent pass, so that the top-level goal can report the records
-- deadlines, which do not depend on qualifying, when qualification cannot
-- be decided.
@ref ss 1(2), 28(1)
GIVEN q IS A `Qualification facts`, civil IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualification can be decided for` q `in civil proceedings` civil IF
        civil
    OR  `is excluded from the national minimum wage` q
    OR  (    (q's `an agency worker within s 34` OR q's `a home worker within s 35` OR known (q's `has a worker's contract`))
         AND (    (    q's `employed on a ship registered in the United Kingdom`
                   AND NOT q's `the employment is wholly outside the United Kingdom`
                   AND q's `ordinarily resident in the United Kingdom`)
              OR  known (q's `working or ordinarily working in the United Kingdom`))
         AND known (q's `has ceased to be of compulsory school age`))
    WHERE
        GIVEN m IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        known m MEANS
            CONSIDER m
            WHEN JUST b  THEN TRUE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
